.TH CSTRING_CREATE_FULL 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cstring_create_full \- create a string with custom memory management
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cstring.h>

cstr cstring_create_full(const char *initial, ccol_memmgmt_procs_t *m_procs,
                         char **err);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function allocates and initialises a new cstring. When initial is
not NULL its content is copied in, and a NULL gives an empty string. The
capacity of the internal buffer is rounded up to the nearest power of two,
and it is at least 16 bytes.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
initial   Initial C string content, or NULL for an empty string
m_procs   Custom memory management procedures, or NULL for the default
          malloc/free. The string keeps its own copy of the structure,
          so yours does not have to outlive the call
err       Optional pointer to receive an error string on failure
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A pointer to the new cstring on success
NULL on failure, with the details written to *err when err is not NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_create (3),
.BR cstring_destroy (3)
